---
/*
  CardCover — the image column of the sitewide card.

  Extracted 2026-08-01, from Jackson: "many of the cards in projects are
  cutting off the map/visual." The three card sites (Home tools strip, Home
  selected projects, the Tools page) and the Projects index each carried
  their own copy of this <Image>, so the crop bug had to be fixed four
  times or it would drift. Now it is fixed once.

  WHAT WAS WRONG. The image column is `sm:w-64` inside a `sm:flex` row and
  had no height of its own, so it stretched to whatever the TEXT column
  measured and `object-cover` filled that box. A 256-wide box against a
  285-tall card is 0.90 — portrait — and every landscape map on the page
  was being sliced down to a portrait strip of itself. The Rooney sheet
  (1.545) kept 44% of its width. AGENTS.md already recorded the symptom
  twice, as the White Sulphur Springs aerial "looking wrong" and as the
  land ownership figure being cut through its own title; `cover.fit` fixed
  the second case by not cropping figures at all. This fixes the cause.

  WHAT REPLACES IT. The box now takes its aspect from THE IMAGE, clamped to
  a range, so no cover is ever cropped by more than the clamp allows:

    ratio 0.85 .. 1.50, from cover.src.width / cover.src.height

  Every cover on the site sits inside that range except the White Sulphur
  Springs aerial (1.778), which loses 16% of its width — it is a
  photograph, and losing its ends costs nothing. Everything else is now
  uncropped: the Rooney hillshade at 1.545 is within a rounding error of
  the ceiling, the stacked school-scenario cover at 0.898 and the
  Arizona-centred estimator crop at 1.077 both land inside untouched. The
  clamp exists so one very tall or very wide cover cannot set the height of
  a whole card.

  WHY THE CLAMP IS 1.50 AND NOT 4:3. 1.50 keeps the Rooney sheets whole.
  A 1.333 ceiling would crop them 14%, which is the kind of quiet loss this
  change exists to stop.

  THE WRAPPER IS NOT DECORATION. `aspect-ratio` on a flex item is ignored
  while the item is being stretched to the row height, which is the default.
  The image therefore sits in a wrapper that takes the stretch and carries
  the divider, and the image is centred inside it. Without the wrapper the
  border between image and text would stop wherever the image stopped, and
  the card would look unfinished on its longer entries.

  `sizes` — READ THE NOTE IN AGENTS.md BEFORE CHANGING THIS. It has to
  describe the width the image is scaled to, which is not the width of the
  box whenever object-cover is cropping horizontally. Worst case on the
  site is now the WSS aerial: box height 256/1.5 = 171px, scaled width
  171 x 1.778 = 303px, so 19rem. It was 32rem before this change, when the
  box could be arbitrarily tall; the aspect ceiling is what makes the
  smaller value correct, and the two must move together.
*/
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import type { ImageMetadata } from 'astro';

interface Props {
	src: ImageMetadata;
	alt: string;
	/** "contain" for a self-contained figure, "cover" for a picture. */
	fit?: 'cover' | 'contain';
	eager?: boolean;
	/**
	 * Column width variant. Added 2026-08-03, Jackson's call, relaxing the
	 * one-card-shape rule to one SHAPE in three SIZES: the Projects index
	 * lets tier 1 run wider and tier 3 tighter, so hierarchy is carried by
	 * presentation as well as by the headings — the same move as leading
	 * tier 3 with Campus at Night via `order`. Every other card site keeps
	 * the default "md", which is exactly the previous rendering.
	 *
	 * `sizes` MOVES WITH THE WIDTH (see the note above): scaled width =
	 * (column / 1.5 clamp) x 1.778 worst-case aspect, so 24rem for the
	 * 20rem column, 19rem for 16rem, 16rem for the 13rem column.
	 */
	size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';
	/**
	 * View-transition name linking this cover to the same image on the
	 * page the card leads to (2026-08-03). Pass `cover-<project.id>` from
	 * card sites whose target page renders the cover with the same name;
	 * the browser then morphs card thumbnail into page cover instead of
	 * hard-cutting. Must be unique per page — never give two cards on one
	 * page the same name. Purely additive: browsers without
	 * cross-document view transitions ignore it.
	 */
	transitionName?: string;
}

const {
	src,
	alt,
	fit = 'cover',
	eager = false,
	size = 'md',
	transitionName,
} = Astro.props;

const BOX_MIN = 0.85;
const BOX_MAX = 1.5;
const box = Math.min(BOX_MAX, Math.max(BOX_MIN, src.width / src.height));

const COLUMN = {
	sm: 'sm:w-52',
	md: 'sm:w-64',
	lg: 'sm:w-80',
}[size];
const SIZES = {
	sm: '(min-width: 640px) 16rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)',
	md: '(min-width: 640px) 19rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)',
	lg: '(min-width: 640px) 24rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)',
}[size];
---

<div
	class:list={[
		'w-full border-b border-line sm:flex sm:shrink-0 sm:items-center sm:border-r sm:border-b-0',
		COLUMN,
	]}
>
	<Image
		src={src}
		alt={alt}
		widths={[320, 640, 1024]}
		sizes={SIZES}
		loading={eager ? 'eager' : 'lazy'}
		style={`--box: ${box.toFixed(4)}${transitionName ? `; view-transition-name: ${transitionName}` : ''}`}
		class:list={[
			'w-full sm:aspect-[var(--box)]',
			fit === 'contain' ? 'object-contain' : 'object-cover',
		]}
	/>
</div>
